WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:01.890
- Welcome to the Huberman Lab Podcast,

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:04.930
where we discuss science
and science-based tools

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:06.114
for everyday life.

00:00:06.114 --> 00:00:09.150
[upbeat music]

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:10.240
I'm Andrew Huberman,

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:13.350
and I'm a professor of
neurobiology and ophthalmology

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:15.310
at Stanford School of Medicine.

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:17.220
Today, we are going to discuss light

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.920
and the many powerful uses of
light to optimize our health.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.730
We're going to discuss the use of light

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:26.310
for optimizing skin health,
appearance, and longevity,

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:29.690
for wound healing, for
optimizing hormone balance,

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:32.730
and for regulating sleep, alertness, mood,

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:35.030
and even for offsetting dementia.

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:37.580
One of the reasons why light
has such powerful effects

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:40.270
on so many different
aspects of our biology

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:43.850
is that it can be translated
into electrical signals

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:45.140
in our brain and body,

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:47.660
into hormone signals
in our brain and body,

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:49.420
and indeed into what we call

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:51.610
cascades of biological pathways,

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:54.770
meaning light can
actually change the genes

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:56.720
that the cells of your bodies express.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:59.170
And that is true throughout the lifespan.

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:00.800
Today, I will discuss the mechanisms

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.660
by which all of that occurs.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:04.520
I promise to make it
clear for those of you

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:06.400
that don't have a biology background.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.350
And if you do have a biology background,

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:10.120
I'll try and provide sufficient depth

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.070
so that it's still of interest to you.

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:14.300
And I promise to give you tools,

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:16.270
very specific protocols that are extracted

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:17.670
from the peer-reviewed literature

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:20.690
that will allow you to use
different so-called wave lengths,

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:22.770
which most of us think of as colors,

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:25.670
of light in order to modulate your health

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:28.030
in the ways that are
most important to you.

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:29.010
For those of you that are thinking

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:30.850
that the use of light to modulate health

00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:32.720
falls under the category of woo science,

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:35.170
pseudoscience, or biohacking,

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:37.860
well, nothing could be
further from the truth.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:42.360
In fact, in 1903, the Nobel
Prize was given to Niels Finsen,

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.750
he was Icelandic, he lived in Denmark,

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:48.850
for the use of phototherapy
for the treatment of lupus.

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:52.180
So there's more than a hundred
years of quality science

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:54.720
emphasizing the use of light,

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:58.420
and as you'll soon see, the
use of particular wavelengths

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:01.920
or colors of light in order
to modulate the activity

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.200
of cells in the brain and body.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:08.060
So while it is the case that
many places and companies

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.410
are selling therapies and products

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:14.560
related to the use of flashing
lights and colored lights,

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:17.260
promising specific
outcomes from everything

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:21.080
from stem cell renewal to
improvement of brain function,

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:24.460
and some of those don't
have any basis in science,

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:28.530
there are photo therapies that
do have a strong foundation

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:29.530
in quality science,

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:31.530
and those are the
studies and the protocols

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.270
that we are going to discuss today.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:36.290
But I thought that people
might appreciate knowing that

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:37.420
over a hundred years ago,

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:39.200
people were thinking
about the use of light

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.670
for the treatment of various diseases

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:41.810
and for improving health.

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:45.130
And indeed many of those
therapies are used today

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:48.570
in high quality hospitals
and research institutions

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:51.150
and, of course, clinics
and homes around the world.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:53.250
One of the more exciting
examples of phototherapy

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:54.540
in the last few years

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:56.520
is the beautiful work of Dr. Glen Jeffery

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:58.260
at University College London.

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:00.300
The Jeffery Lab is known
for doing pioneering

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:01.380
and very rigorous research

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:03.450
in the realm of visual neuroscience.

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:04.710
And in the last decade or so,

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:07.020
they turned their attention
to exploring the role

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:11.780
of red light therapy for
offsetting age-related vision loss.

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:15.100
What they discovered is
that just brief exposures

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:17.000
to red light early in the day

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.960
can offset much of the vision loss

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:21.890
that occurs in people 40 years or older.

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:23.810
And what's remarkable about these studies

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:26.590
is that the entire duration of the therapy

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:28.010
is just one to three minutes,

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:30.130
done just a few times per week.

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:31.400
What's even more exciting

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.010
is that they understand the mechanism

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:35.000
by which this occurred.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.300
The cells in the back of the eye

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:39.230
that convert light information
into electrical signals

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:41.050
that the rest of the brain can understand

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:42.840
and create visual images from,

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:46.060
well, those cells are
extremely metabolically active.

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:49.870
They need a lot of ATP or energy.

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.390
And as we age,

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:53.570
those cells get less efficient

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:56.370
at creating that ATP and energy.

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:58.990
Exposure to red light early in the day,

00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:01.090
and it does have to be early in the day,

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:03.960
allowed those cells to
replenish the mechanisms

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:05.980
by which they create ATP.

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:07.700
I'll talk about these experiments

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:09.360
in more detail later in the episode

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:12.010
and the protocols so that you
could apply those protocols

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:13.130
should you choose.

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:17.750
But I use this as an example
of our growing understanding

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:22.030
of not just that phototherapies
work but how they work.

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:25.870
And it is through the linking
of protocols and mechanism

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:28.140
that we, meaning all of us,

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:29.670
can start to apply phototherapies

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:32.450
in a rational, safe, and powerful way.

